Keeps the Canon EOS 2000D running as a remote astro instrument — the big-sensor, real-optics complement to the Pi cameras.

The Canon EOS 2000D as a remotely-operated astro instrument, tethered over USB to muppet via gphoto2. The big-sensor, real-optics complement to the Pi cameras (astrocam, eclipticam): 24 MP APS-C, EF-S 18-55 zoom, remote focus drive. Weather-gated — each visit is typically "PSU/battery + clear night + run the tools, then improve them".
